Revision history for Net-Async-Hetzner

RELEASE COUPLING: This distribution reuses WWW::Hetzner's private
_build_request/_parse_response and MUST be released together with
WWW::Hetzner (repo p5-www-hetzner). Never release Net-Async-Hetzner
alone; coordinate both releases through a karr ticket. See CLAUDE.md and
.claude/rules/net-async-hetzner-rules.md for the protocol.

{{$NEXT}}
    - Robot: get/post/put/delete now check credentials up front and croak
      "No Robot credentials configured" instead of sending empty Basic auth
    - Cloud/Robot: configure() drops the cached WWW::Hetzner client so new
      token/credentials/base_url take effect
    - cpanfile: require IO::Async::SSL (both default endpoints are https),
      WWW::Hetzner 0.102 (the sibling these tests run against)
    - Net::Async::HTTP is loaded with use instead of a late require
    - Cloud/Robot: new `timeout` attribute (default 30s, 0 = none); stalled requests
      now fail their Future instead of staying pending forever
    - POD: Robot post/put are form-encoded, not JSON; document croak on missing credentials
    - Tests: expect URL-encoded query values (label_selector=env%3Dprod)

0.003     2026-02-12 17:23:03Z
    - Initial release
    - Net::Async::Hetzner::Cloud - async Cloud API client
    - Net::Async::Hetzner::Robot - async Robot API client
    - IO::Async integration via IO::Async::Notifier
    - Future-based async HTTP methods (get, post, put, delete)
    - Reuses WWW::Hetzner _build_request/_parse_response for request/response logic
    - Net::Async::HTTP for non-blocking transport
    - Basic Auth support for Robot API
